>> Play Tennis: a multiway root and different questions below it

`id3_tennis()` retains the original fourteen-row teaching fixture. It is constructed
categorical data, not a measured weather study. Outlook uses sunny/overcast/rain
codes 0/1/2; temperature hot/mild/cool uses 0/1/2; humidity high/normal uses 0/1;
windy false/true uses 0/1; the class play uses no/yes codes 0/1.

There are nine yes and five no labels, so the root entropy is
\(h_2(9/14)=0.9402859587\). Outlook's child class counts are sunny (2 yes,3 no),
overcast (4 yes,0 no), and rain (3 yes,2 no). Therefore

$$
 G(S,\text{outlook})=h_2(9/14)-\frac5{14}h_2(2/5)
 -\frac4{14}\,0-\frac5{14}h_2(3/5)=0.2467498198.
$$
\alttext(Outlook's gain is root entropy minus five fourteenths of sunny entropy, four fourteenths of the pure overcast entropy and five fourteenths of rain entropy. It equals about 0.246750 bits.)

This exceeds humidity's 0.151836, wind's 0.048127 and temperature's 0.029223 bits.
Sunny rows next ask humidity; rain rows ask wind. Overcast rows stop immediately.
The node table reports the majority fallback even on internal nodes, and uses
feature -1 for leaves. A leaf's feature field is not a test.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/id3_tennis.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace a     = dm::algorithms;
  const auto d    = a::id3_tennis();
  const auto tree = a::id3_train(d.features, d.labels);
  const auto s    = a::id3_split_table(d.features, d.labels, d.feature_names);
  auto       gains =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(
          s.numeric_column("gain").values(), d.feature_names, "gain (bits)", {50, 100, 190})
          .title("Root candidate gains")
          .x_label("candidate attribute")
          .y_label("gain (bits)")
          .y_limits(0, .3);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(gains)
      .add(a::plot_id3_tree(tree, d.feature_names))
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/id3_tennis.svg");
  std::print(
      "Root candidates\n\n{}\n\nOutlook branches\n\n{}\n\nTree nodes\n\n{}\n\nTraining fit\n\n{}\n",
      s.to_md(),
      a::id3_branch_table(d.features, d.labels, 0).to_md(),
      a::id3_node_table(tree).to_md(),
      a::id3_evaluate(tree, d.features, d.labels).to_md());
}
