> Observed data: Titanic passenger survival

`dm::datasets::titanic()` supplies the bundled 891-row, 12-column Kaggle training
set. We select Sex, Pclass, Embarked and Survived, then remove the two rows missing
Embarked, retaining 889 rows. Missing Age and Cabin values are irrelevant to these
selected columns. Pclass is a three-level category here, not a continuous measure.
The response is Survived, coded zero or one. PassengerId, names, tickets and cabins
are excluded; the identifier example explains one reason for excluding identifiers.

Before fitting, declare a deterministic split: positions divisible by five in the
retained dataset, counting from zero, are the 178 holdout rows; the other 711 rows
are fitting rows. This is a transparent demonstration split, without stratification,
family grouping, repeated evaluation or population uncertainty estimates. It does
not establish transport to another passenger population or separate related families.

Fix maximum depth two before looking at holdout results. The DataFrame wrapper learns
its dictionaries on the fitting rows only. New levels encode as -1, which cannot
collide with learned nonnegative codes, and follow the same local-majority rule.
Predictor column names and types are checked at inference; column order may differ.
Nulls and nonfinite values are rejected, rather than converted to classes or silently
removed. Integer-valued labels are required. Numeric values remain categories even
when their magnitudes suggest an ordering.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/id3_titanic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace a         = dm::algorithms;
  const auto selected = dm::datasets::titanic().select({"Sex", "Pclass", "Embarked", "Survived"});
  const auto complete = selected.drop_nulls();
  std::vector<std::size_t> fit_rows, test_rows;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < complete.nrows(); ++i)
    (i % 5 == 0 ? test_rows : fit_rows).push_back(i);
  const auto fit = complete.take_rows(fit_rows), test = complete.take_rows(test_rows);
  const std::vector<std::string> predictors{"Sex", "Pclass", "Embarked"};
  const a::ID3FrameClassifier    model(fit, predictors, "Survived", 2);
  const auto train_result = model.evaluate(fit), test_result = model.evaluate(test);
  const a::ID3FrameClassifier stump(fit, predictors, "Survived", 1);
  const auto                  values = fit.numeric_column("Survived").values();
  const std::vector<int>      labels(values.begin(), values.end());
  const auto                  gains = a::id3_split_table(model.encode(fit), labels, predictors);
  auto                        score =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .bars(
              {0, 1},
              {train_result.double_at("accuracy", 0), test_result.double_at("accuracy", 0)},
              "tree",
              {40, 100, 190},
              .22)
          .bars(
              {.25, 1.25},
              {train_result.double_at("baseline_accuracy", 0),
               test_result.double_at("baseline_accuracy", 0)},
              "majority",
              {180, 100, 40},
              .22)
          .title("Predeclared depth-two evaluation")
          .x_label("0 = fitting; 1 = holdout")
          .y_label("accuracy")
          .x_limits(-.4, 1.65)
          .y_limits(0, 1.15)
          .legend({"tree", "majority"}, {{40, 100, 190}, {180, 100, 40}});
  auto gain_plot =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(
          gains.numeric_column("gain").values(), predictors, "gain (bits)", {40, 100, 190})
          .title("Root gains from fitting rows only")
          .x_label("candidate attribute")
          .y_label("gain (bits)")
          .y_limits(0, .3);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(gain_plot)
      .add(score)
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/id3_titanic.svg");
  std::print(
      "Depth-one and depth-two holdout labels agree: {}.\n\n",
      stump.predict(test) == model.predict(test));
  std::print(
      "Selected {} of 891 rows; omitted {} incomplete rows. Fitting {}, holdout {}.\n\nFitting-row "
      "root gains\n\n{}\n\nFitting evaluation\n\n{}\n\nHoldout evaluation\n\n{}\n\nFitted "
      "nodes\n\n{}\n",
      complete.nrows(),
      selected.nrows() - complete.nrows(),
      fit.nrows(),
      test.nrows(),
      gains.to_md(),
      train_result.to_md(),
      test_result.to_md(),
      a::id3_node_table(model.tree()).to_md());
}
```
